The '''2024–25 season''' was the 127th season in the history of '''[[Athletic Bilbao]]''', and the club's 94th consecutive season in [[La Liga]].<ref>[https://www.bdfutbol.com/en/t/t2024-256.html Squad of Athletic Club 2024-25 First Division], BDFutbol</ref> In addition to the [[2024–25 La Liga|domestic league]], the club also participated in the [[2024–25 Copa del Rey|Copa del Rey]], the [[2025 Supercopa de España|Supercopa de España]] (after winning the [[2023–24 Copa del Rey]]), and the [[2024–25 UEFA Europa League|UEFA Europa League]] (competing [[Athletic Bilbao in European football|in Europe]] for the first time in seven years).

Following a 2–0 victory over [[Getafe CF|Getafe]] in the 36th round of La Liga, Athletic Bilbao successfully qualified for the [[UEFA Champions League]] for the first time since the [[2014–15 UEFA Champions League|2014–15 season]].

== Summary ==
On 13 June, midfielder [[Ander Herrera]] had his contract renewed until the year 2025.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.athletic-club.eus/en/news/2024/06/13/ander-herrera-extends-his-contract-with-athletic-club/|title=Ander Herrera extends his contract with Athletic Club|publisher=Athletic Bilbao|date=13 June 2024}}</ref>

